WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:01.901
-Hi, everybody.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.569
Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.172
My name is Jimmy Fallon, and
thank you so much for watching.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.907
We have a great show
for you tonight.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:11.110
Guys, I want to wish everyone
a happy "Star Wars" Day.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.611
That's right --
it's a time fans say,

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:14.547
"May the 4th be with you,"

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.883
which is great, because now
you know what day it is.

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:19.385
Yep, they call it
"Star Wars" Day because of

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.787
the phrase "May the 4th
be with you,"

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.190
which, as we know,
was how Baby Yoda said it

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.460
before his front teeth grew in.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.129
Meanwhile,
tomorrow is Cinco de Mayo,

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:31.664
though, right now
Americans are thinking,

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.699
"Yeah, like we need
an excuse to sit around

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.835
drinking tequila all day long."

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:38.004
Check this out.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.239
I heard that doctors and
dentists have now started

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.675
removing magazines
from their waiting room.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.076
Patients were like, "Oh, no.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:47.080
Now how will I find out who was
named Sexiest Man Alive

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.450
in 1997?"

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:56.789
"Brad Pitt and Jennifer Aniston
are breaking up?"

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:59.558
Now airlines are removing their
in-flight magazines.

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:01.227
So now you're going to have to
find somewhere else

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.295
to see a filled-out
Sudoku puzzle

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.398
and stick your wad of gum.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.266
I saw that the new
"Twilight" book

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:09.802
is being released
from Edward's perspective.

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.470
Yep. Women are so excited,
they're like,

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:15.308
"Finally, something from
a male perspective."

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:16.442
I read that,
for the first time,

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.845
murder hornets have been
spotted in the U.S.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.815
So if a worldwide pandemic
can't keep you inside,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:27.020
introducing murder hornets.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.688
Yep, these murder hornets
sound pretty scary,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.056
so we wanted to find out more.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:33.092
Joining us now,
one of the murder hornets.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.427
Thank you for being here.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.595
-Jimmy! What's up, man?
How you doing?

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:37.697 line:0%
-I'm good.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.265 line:0%
Thanks for letting me
talk to you here.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.767 line:0%
I got to say,
you sound pretty friendly

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.704 line:0%
for something that's called
a murder hornet.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.239
-Murder hornet? Really?

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.373
Is that what
they're calling us now?

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.542
Look, we're just
regular old bees

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.945
who happen to make things
fall asleep forever.

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:55.114
-Right, but I heard that you've
just been discovered

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:58.417
in our country and that you've
been decapitating our bees.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.453
-Decapi-what?! No, man.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.422
We're just rough-housing
with your boys.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.357
We practice MMA moves
on each other.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.058
-MMA?

00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:09.995
-But sometimes, you know, that
horseplay goes a little south.

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:11.497
But it's all in good fun.

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:14.200
You know, the news isn't always
so black and yellow, you know.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.669
-But they're saying
bee-keeper suits

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.338
can't even protect humans
from your stingers, though.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:22.274
-Bee-keeper suits also don't
protect you from drowning,

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:25.344
but I don't hear you calling
the ocean "murder water."

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:27.379
-I guess that makes sense.

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:28.815
-You know, you jump
in front of a bus

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.016
with a bee-keeper suit on,
and they're not going to call it

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:32.352
a "murder bus."

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.621
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I get your point there.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:37.123
-You just got stung, Jimmy.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.592
-Okay. Look, if you don't want
to be called murder hornets,

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.394
what do you want to be called?

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:42.929
-Ooh! I'm just
spit-balling here.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:46.299
Maybe, um...spicy bees?

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.802 line:0%
-Spicy bees?

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.871 line:0%
-Yeah, grumpy bugs.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:55.275 line:0%
Little fellas who woke up on
the wrong side of the bed.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.477 line:0%
Hornets who do murder sometimes.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.779
Butterflies, but instead
of butterflies,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:00.847
they're murder hornets.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.015
-Alright, alright.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.383
I'm glad we got to
the bottom of all that.

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:06.352
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.619
-My pleasure, Jimmy.

00:03:07.619 --> 00:03:10.022
Also, quick shout-out
to my crisis P.R. team,

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:11.524
HWC &amp; Associates.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.327
I owe them everything.
I'd be nowhere without them.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:17.563
Alright, I got to go do some
"MMA moves" on your honeybees.

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:19.098
Murder hornet out!

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.700
-Thank you very much,
grumpy bug.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.801
We have a great show tonight.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.136
Ashton Kutcher and
Mila Kunis are here.

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:26.472 line:0%
They're going to talk to us
about quarantine wine.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.740 line:0%
This is their wine
that they have

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.643 line:0%
where all profits go to
four separate charities

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.012 line:0%
for COVID-19 relief.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.246 line:0%
It's kind of an amazing idea,

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:36.949 line:0%
and they pulled it off in
perfect amount of time.

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:39.319 line:0%
I also like that
the label is blank

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.954 line:0%
so you can write
who you're thankful for

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.989 line:0%
or what you're thankful for

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.825 line:0%
while you're having
a little quarantine wine.

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:48.561
Also, we have Evan Rachel Wood
from "Westworld."

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:49.962
Just --
The finale was last night.

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:52.264
She's going to talk a little bit
about that, but no spoilers.

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:53.933
And then we're just going to see
what else she's up to.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.935
I believe she's learning
how to play piano.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.102
She's that amazing.

00:03:57.102 --> 00:04:00.106
And we have great music tonight.
Oh, my goodness.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.941
She's one of my
all-time favorites.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.175
Honey --
-I'm freaking out.

00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:05.345
-I know.
We've just been playing --

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.745
-We have been playing
that album --

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:08.181
-"Diva."
-"Diva."

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:11.950
-Over and over again.
Annie Lennox. Oh!

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.053
I want Annie Lennox on the show
every single night.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.389
I love everything about her.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.791
I think she's the coolest human.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.792
She came on our show
a couple years ago --

00:04:20.792 --> 00:04:23.862
no entourage, just walked in,
Annie Lennox, had a book.

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:25.531
That was her entourage --
a book.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.565
A dog-eared book.

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:28.734
And I go,
"Can I get you anything?"

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.903
She's just that cool.
I just love her.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.972 line:0%
She's going to talk about this
thing called Project Angel Food,

00:04:33.972 --> 00:04:36.942 line:0%
which delivers meals to
people in Los Angeles

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:38.176 line:0%
who are seriously ill.

00:04:38.176 --> 00:04:39.478 line:0%
It's a beautiful charity.

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:40.579 line:0%
And she's going to sing a song

00:04:40.579 --> 00:04:42.415 line:0%
for us tonight
with her amazing voice.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.216
I love you, Annie Lennox,
so much.

00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:45.517
This is so fun.

00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:50.289 line:0%
Also, I want to say
Mick Jagger is here

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:54.093 line:0%
on behalf of
savethechildren.org.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:57.230 line:0%
Please go to that website
and do whatever you can.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.431 line:0%
We would love that,
and thank you so much.

